  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PNG Smarter Safer Schools</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The PNG Smarter Safer Schools Program (SSS) has been developed jointly by the UNICEF and DFAT to support the Government of PNG (GoPNG) to improve access to and the quality and safety of learning for students in early childhood and basic education. It seeks to support PNG&#x2019;s goals for implementing the &#x201c;1-6-6&#x201d; education system  (refer to Annexes) and improve timely enrolment, retention, completion and learning outcomes, and build the education system&#x2019;s resilience to respond to risks from natural, climate-related and humanitarian crises that disrupt learning. SSS&#x2019;s End-of-Program Outcomes are focused on:
1.	Learner safety and well-being through Learning and Skills Development, especially for adolescent girls
2.	Resilience building and climate change adaptation in education.
3.	Strengthened sector planning, coordination and management information systems for improved efficiency.
4.	Quality education and school standards through the 1-6-6 restructure.</narrative>
  </description>
